window.SITE = {"dob": "2026-01-11", "name": "Ḥanzalā", "weeks": "<h1 class=\"h1\">Hanzala — 52 Weeks, One Islamic Year<\/h1>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">5 September 2026 → 5 September 2027 (his age: 7 months → 19 months)<\/h3>\n<p><b>Family style:<\/b> traditional / tasawwuf-leaning · <b>Languages at home:<\/b> English + Urdu/Hindi Companion files: <code>TOY-AND-STUDY-PLAN.md<\/code> (toys &amp; avoid-list by age) · <code>FRIDGE-CHECKLIST.md<\/code> (one-page tick list)<\/p>\n<blockquote><b>Rule of the year:<\/b> one āyah, one word, one sunnah habit, one toy, one walk — <b>each week<\/b>. Nothing more. A 19-month-old who says <i>Bismillāh<\/i>, <i>Allāh<\/i>, <i>duʿāʾ<\/i>, <i>āmīn<\/i>, <i>sajdah<\/i> and claps at the sound of the adhān has been taught more than a child pushed to memorise under pressure.<\/blockquote>\n<p><b>Two calendar notes for you:<\/b><\/p>\n<ul><li>12 Rabīʿ al-Awwal 1448 (South Asia) was <b>26 August 2026<\/b> — Mawlid has just passed. Don't chase it; the next is <b>Sunday 15 August 2027<\/b> = Week 50.<\/li><li>All Hijri dates below are ±1 day. <b>Follow your local masjid's moon sighting<\/b>, especially for Ramaḍān and the two ʿĪds.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p><b>One thing — the only thing that decides whether this works:<\/b> 20 minutes of you on the floor, phone in another room, five days a week. Not the toys.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">13 dates to circle in your calendar (planning dates — confirm with your masjid)<\/h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Date (2026–27)<\/th><th>Event<\/th><th>Where it sits here<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>27 Rajab 1448 ≈ <b>5 Jan 27<\/b><\/td><td>Shab-e-Merāj (no infant rite)<\/td><td>Wk 13–14<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>11 Jan 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>His 1st year — shukr day, not a party<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 19<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>~24 Jan 27<\/td><td>Laylat al-Barāʾah (15 Shaʿbān)<\/td><td>Wk 21<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>8 Feb 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>1 Ramaḍān 1448<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 23–24<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6 Mar 27<\/td><td>27th night — Qadr<\/td><td>Wk 26<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>9–10 Mar 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>ʿĪd al-Fiṭr<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 28<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>15 May 27<\/td><td>Yawm ʿArafah (9 Dhū al-Ḥijjah)<\/td><td>Wk 36–37<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>16 May 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>ʿĪd al-Aḍḥā + qurbānī<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 38<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>6 Jun 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>1 Muharram 1449 — new Hijri year<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 41<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>15 Jun 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>ʿĀshūrāʾ — his first \"game-fast\"<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 42<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>~2 Jul 27<\/td><td>Start of the 25th month from birth; no ritual for Ṣafar (see note on amulets, Wk 44)<\/td><td>Wk 44<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>15 Aug 27<\/b><\/td><td><b>12 Rabīʿ al-Awwal 1449 — Mawlid<\/b><\/td><td><b>Wk 50<\/b><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>12 Rabiʿ 1448 — 26 Aug 26<\/td><td>Mawlid <b>already passed<\/b> — nothing to do<\/td><td>—<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">A. The fixed weekly frame (same shape all 52 weeks)<\/h2>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Day<\/th><th>20–30 min slot<\/th><th>Muslim content<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Saturday<\/b><\/td><td>Water / sand / outdoor<\/td><td>ṣadaqah tin, feed the birds, \"SubḥānAllāh\" at what he sees<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>Sunday<\/b><\/td><td>Floor play + rhythm<\/td><td>ḥamd/naʿt with clapping and ḍuff only, dancing with Abū<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>Monday<\/b><\/td><td>Books + quiet<\/td><td>1 board book + the week's āyah aloud<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>Tuesday<\/b><\/td><td>Skills<\/td><td>crawl/walk obstacle, cups, pincer (thumb-finger) games<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>Wednesday<\/b><\/td><td><b>Raḥmah<\/b><\/td><td>gentle with doll, cat, ants; share 2 biscuits; soft voice<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>Thursday<\/b><\/td><td><b>Silaṭ ar-raḥim<\/b><\/td><td>grandparents, phone call, plate to the neighbour<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><b>Friday<\/b><\/td><td><b>Jumuʿah identity<\/b><\/td><td>ghusl + thobe, masjid visit (he can play at the edge), sūrah al-Kahf in the house, special lunch, nails/hair not cut before he returns<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Daily, no exceptions:<\/b> Bismillāh before food · Alḥamdulillāh after · 10 min Qurʾān audible · morning &amp; evening adhkār · duʿāʾ using his name · <b>zero screens.<\/b><\/p>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">B. Week-by-week<\/h2>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 1 — Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 1448 · Wks 1–4 · 5 Sep–4 Oct 2026 · <b>7 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: al-ḥamdu lillāh (शुक्र / شکر)<\/b> · <b>Ism of Allāh: al-Wāḥid الواحد<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah of the week<\/th><th>New words (AR / UR-HI / EN)<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>1<\/td><td>5–11 Sep<\/td><td>al-Fātiḥah 1–2<\/td><td>Allāh / اللہ / God<\/td><td>Sit him facing you; say \"Allāh\" 20×, one clap each time. Record it, play it at Ẓuhr.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>12–18 Sep<\/td><td>al-Fātiḥah 3–4<\/td><td>alḥamdulillāh / الحمد لله<\/td><td>Every bite: \"Bismillāh\" before, \"Alḥamdulillāh\" finished. He watches your mouth — that's how he learns.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>19–25 Sep<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Ikhlāṣ<\/td><td>ustad / استاد · teacher<\/td><td>Roll the ball to him; when it comes back: \"Allāhu akbar!\" Return = joy, the first social game.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>26 Sep–2 Oct<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Kawthar<\/td><td>pānī / पानी · water<\/td><td><b>New toy: 3 hole-free bath cups.<\/b> Water play + the ḥadīth of the thirsty dog, in 3 sentences.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Check:<\/b> sits without support ~1 min · rolls both ways · laughs aloud · turns to his name <b>Abū's task:<\/b> pray 2 rakʿah in the same room with him awake, 3× a week — he must <i>see<\/i> you bow.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 2 — Jumādā al-Ūlā 1448 · Wks 5–8 · 3–30 Oct 2026 · <b>8–9 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: ʿaqīqah &amp; his name<\/b> · <b>Ism: as-Salām السلام<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>5<\/td><td>3–9 Oct<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Falaq<\/td><td>ʿaqīqah / عقیقہ<\/td><td>If the 7th-day ʿaqīqah (2 sheep for a boy — sunnah) was missed, do it now, any day. Say his name at the duʿāʾ of the sacrifice; ⅓ to the poor.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>10–16 Oct<\/td><td>Sūrah an-Nās<\/td><td>kaun / कौन · who?<\/td><td><b>New toy: soft fabric mirror.<\/b> \"Kaun hai? — Ḥanzalā!\" Point, name, smile.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td>17–23 Oct<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Fīl<\/td><td>dāhāṇā / दाहिना · right<\/td><td>Right hand for eating: put food in his right hand every single time, say \"dāhāṇā\".<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>8<\/td><td>24–30 Oct<\/td><td>Sūrah Quraysh<\/td><td>nīlā / नीला · blue<\/td><td><b>New toy: 4 wooden rings / coloured rattles.<\/b> Name the colour + \"SubḥānAllāh\" each.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Check:<\/b> bears weight on legs · crawls or drags · pincer grasp · \"mama/dada\" babble · peek-a-boo understood <b>Avoid:<\/b> Diwālī cracker toys and puja-style gift items. If relatives bring them, one kind sentence and into the drawer — no argument.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 3 — Jumādā al-Ākhira 1448 · Nov 2026 · <b>9–10 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: raḥmah — mercy to every living thing<\/b> · <b>Ism: ar-Raḥīm الرحيم<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>9<\/td><td>31 Oct–6 Nov<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Lahab<\/td><td>jānvar / जानवर · animal<\/td><td>The cat and the dog stories (2 min). Put a crumb for the ants <i>with<\/i> his hand.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>10<\/td><td>7–13 Nov<\/td><td>Sūrah an-Naṣr<\/td><td>āmīn / آمین<\/td><td>Teach <b>āmīn<\/b>: you duʿā out loud \"Allāhummaḥfaẓ Ḥanzalā\" → he says \"āmīn\". The key skill of this month.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>11<\/td><td>14–20 Nov<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Kāfirūn<\/td><td>goḍiyā / गुड़िया · doll<\/td><td><b>New toy: soft doll + blanket.<\/b> <i>You<\/i> stroke it first, then hand it to him: \"naram, naram\".<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>12<\/td><td>21–27 Nov<\/td><td>Sūrah at-Takāthur<\/td><td>nahlānā / नहलाना · bath<\/td><td>Bath = splash + \"Allāhu akbar\". Let him wash his own face: ṭahārah as a happy habit, not a rule.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Check:<\/b> pulls to stand · waves bye-bye · puts a cube in a cup · knows \"nahi\" · claps <b>Qurʾān at this age:<\/b> you recite, he hears. Loop al-Falaq, an-Nās, al-Ikhlāṣ at sleep. Do <b>not<\/b> attempt reading or flash-cards — at 10 months they teach nothing except that books are boring.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 4 — Rajab 1448 · Dec 2026 · <b>11 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: the gift of ṣalāh made visible<\/b> · <b>Ism: al-Muḥyī المحيي<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>13<\/td><td>28 Nov–4 Dec<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Isrāʾ 1<\/td><td>namāz / नमाज़<\/td><td>Lay <i>his<\/i> small rug next to yours. At your sujud, rest his forehead down once, then \"MāshāAllāh!\" Never force.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>14<\/td><td>5–11 Dec<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Muzzammil 1–10<\/td><td>qayām<\/td><td>Once this month, wake 3 min before Fajr with him; hand on his head; duʿāʾ in Urdu/Hindi.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>15<\/td><td>12–18 Dec<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Qadr<\/td><td>rozā / रोज़ा<\/td><td>Say the word now so it's ordinary by Ramaḍān: \"Allāh kā rozā\" — and when you drink, \"Alḥamdulillāh\".<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>16<\/td><td>19–25 Dec<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Fātiḥah (review)<\/td><td>qurṭā / कुर्ता<\/td><td><b>New toy: 6 stacking cups + push-trolley<\/b> (not a walker). No Christmas tree/snowman toys — take gifts with a smile, keep in the cupboard.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>17<\/td><td>26 Dec–1 Jan<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Muzzammil (review)<\/td><td>salām / सलाम<\/td><td><b>1 Jan:<\/b> no party. Night of ḥisāb — 2 rakʿah shukr, Sūrah al-Mulk, write his duʿāʾ for the coming year. (The <i>sunnah<\/i> year starts in June — Week 42.)<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Check:<\/b> cruises along furniture · first word likely · imitates gestures · finds a hidden toy <b>27 Rajab ≈ 5 Jan 2027 (Shab-e-Merāj):<\/b> nothing special for an infant. The real benefit of Rajab is that your ṣalāh is now visible to him daily — that's the sīrah lesson.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 5 — Shaʿbān 1448 · Jan 2027 · <b>12 months + birthday 11 Jan<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: shukr for one year, and parents' duʿāʾ<\/b> · <b>Ism: ash-Shakūr الشكور<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>18<\/td><td>2–8 Jan<\/td><td>al-Fātiḥah (full)<\/td><td>Ummī / أمي · mom<\/td><td>\"Ummī, Ummī\" games ×10 daily. The day she is thanked by him will be his ṣalāh.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>19<\/td><td><b>9–15 Jan — 11 Jan: 1 year<\/b><\/td><td>Sūrah aḍ-Ḍuḥā<\/td><td>shukrānā<\/td><td><b>No cake-party — a shukr day:<\/b> you fast; feed one family one meal; write the <i>duʿāʾ letter<\/i> (\"Yā Allāh, make Ḥanzalā a ḥāfiẓ of Your book…\"); recite aḍ-Ḍuḥā: <i>\"wa ammā bi-niʿmati rabbika fa-ḥaddith.\"<\/i> Print one photo, file it under his name.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>20<\/td><td>16–22 Jan<\/td><td>Sūrah ash-Sharḥ<\/td><td>bhookh / भूख<\/td><td>Two cups, two biscuits: \"ek tum, ek Ummī\". Sharing practised now = no greed lecture at 8.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>21<\/td><td>23–29 Jan<\/td><td>Sūrah at-Tīn<\/td><td>dān / दान · give<\/td><td><b>Shab-e-Barat ≈ 24 Jan:<\/b> no ritual for the baby; you pray 2 rakʿah and add his name to your night duʿāʾ. Teach later: we ask <i>only<\/i> Allāh.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>22<\/td><td>30 Jan–5 Feb<\/td><td>Sūrah al-ʿAlaq 1–5<\/td><td>iqrā / इक़रा · read<\/td><td><b>New toy: chunky crayons + paper taped to the wall.<\/b> Free scribble; you name what his scribble \"is\".<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Check:<\/b> stands alone a few seconds · 1 real word · points with index finger · walks holding one hand · drinks from an open cup <b>Ramaḍān starts Mon 8 Feb — prep this week:<\/b> dates jar, his own tiny plate, and tell the family he \"joins\" suḥūr and iftār without fasting.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 6 — RAMAḌĀN 1448 · 8 Feb – 9 Mar 2027 · <b>13 months — the best month of the year<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: the house becomes a madrasah<\/b> · <b>Ism: al-Ghaffūr الغفور<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>23<\/td><td>30 Jan–6 Feb (Ramaḍān from Mon 8 Feb)<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Baqarah 183 (you recite)<\/td><td>Ramaḍān / रमज़ान<\/td><td>First suḥūr: wake him 10 min, one date on the tongue, water, \"Bismillāh\", \"Allāhu akbar\", back to sleep. This one memory is worth a hundred toys.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>24<\/td><td>7–13 Feb<\/td><td>Sūrah an-Naba<\/td><td>ifṭār / इफ़्तार<\/td><td>His job: hand you the date and the glass. \"JazākAllāhu khayran\" — teach the thank-you of the dīn.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>25<\/td><td>14–20 Feb<\/td><td>Sūrah ash-Shams<\/td><td>duʿā / दुआ<\/td><td>After the Maghrib adhān he says \"āmīn\" with you. Tarāwīḥ: 15 min at the masjid, playing at the edge — that counts.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>26<\/td><td>21 Feb–6 Mar (odd nights, 27th ≈ Sat 6 Mar)<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Inshirāḥ<\/td><td>ṣadaqah / दान<\/td><td>Odd nights, esp. <b>27th ≈ Sat 6 Mar:<\/b> put his hand in the ṣadaqah box so he \"gives\". Quiet house, low lights, early sleep — no all-night show.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>27<\/td><td>6–12 Mar<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Bayyinah<\/td><td>zakāh / ज़कात<\/td><td><b>New toy: play food + mini broom.<\/b> He \"helps\" clean: the fiqh of service enters through the hands.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>28<\/td><td><b>ʿĪd al-Fiṭr ≈ 9–10 Mar<\/b><\/td><td>Sūrah al-Aʿlā<\/td><td>ʿīd / ईद<\/td><td>Ghusl + new clothes; Zakāh al-Fiṭr paid in his name — say \"Ḥanzalā kī taraf se, Allāh qabūl farmāye\"; sevāīyā on the tongue; neighbour visits; one photo for the \"ʿĪd wall\".<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Ramaḍān rules for a 13-month-old:<\/b> no screens (kids' channels are full of music and junk), no extra sugar, keep his sleep routine, don't wake him every night, and no adult \"tricks\" that make fasting look like punishment. <b>His Ramaḍān word target (3 words only):<\/b> <i>Allāh · duʿā · āmīn.<\/i> In a Hindi-speaking home keep Islamic terms in Arabic/Urdu — say <b>Allāh<\/b>, not a translated devotional word, so from the start the name of tawḥīd is unmistakable.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 7 — Shawwāl 1448 · Mar 2027 · <b>14 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: lawful joy (no music-party), 6 days of Shawwāl later<\/b> · <b>Ism: al-Fattāḥ الفتاح<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>29<\/td><td>13–19 Mar<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Aʿlā<\/td><td>ḥalāl / हलाल<\/td><td>Play day: water, park, sand, family. Ḥamd/naʿt with clapping and ḍuff only.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>30<\/td><td>20–26 Mar<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Ghāshiyah<\/td><td>khushī / खुशी · happy<\/td><td>The two ʿīds get one phrase: \"ʿĪd mubārak\" — he'll return it before he is 2.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>31<\/td><td>27 Mar–2 Apr<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Māʿūn<\/td><td>jhūth / झूठ · lie<\/td><td>Truth month starts: never scare him with \"Allāh will punish you\", never \"bhūt\" or \"chūhā\" as threats. At 14 months his heart cannot carry fear of Allāh — only love and raḥmah.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 8 — Dhū al-Qaʿdah 1448 · Apr 2027 · <b>15 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: ḥayāʾ and the guard of the eyes<\/b> · <b>Ism: as-Satīr الستير<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>32<\/td><td>3–9 Apr<\/td><td>Sūrah an-Nūr 30 (recite; don't explain)<\/td><td>pardā / परदा<\/td><td>Ḥayāʾ for a toddler is simple: no nakedness before others, door closed, \"logon ke saamne nahi\". The body is amānah.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>33<\/td><td>10–16 Apr<\/td><td>Sūrah al-ʿĀdiyāt<\/td><td>gend / गेंद · ball<\/td><td>Chase, kick, throw outside 30 min/day. A tired body = a calm heart at bedtime.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>34<\/td><td>17–23 Apr<\/td><td>Sūrah az-Zalzalah<\/td><td>pāudhā / पौधा · plant<\/td><td><b>New toy: shape sorter + wooden blocks (40).<\/b> Sow one seed in a cup; \"al-Khāliq ne banāyā\" every morning it grows.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>35<\/td><td>24–30 Apr<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Qāriʿah<\/td><td>sonā / सोना · sleep<\/td><td>Sunnah sleep: 3 Qul + Āyat al-Kursī, blow over him, right side, qiblah side. No phone rocking, no TV lullaby.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p><b>Check (15 mo):<\/b> walks alone · 3–10 words · follows one instruction with a gesture · drinks from a cup without spilling all of it<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 9 — Dhū al-Ḥijjah 1448 · <b>ʿArafah Sat 15 May · ʿĪd al-Aḍḥā Sun 16 May 2027<\/b> · <b>16 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: the ḥajj in our sandbox<\/b> · <b>Ism: al-Akbar الأكبر<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>36<\/td><td>1–7 May<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Ḥajj 27<\/td><td>Kaʿbah / क़ाबा<\/td><td>Build the Kaʿbah from blocks/sand. Walk around it 3× with him: \"Labbayk Allāhumma labbayk\". He'll shout \"labbayk\". Best free activity of the year.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>37<\/td><td>8–14 May<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Kawthar 2<\/td><td>qurbānī / क़ुरबानी<\/td><td>10 Dhū al-Ḥijjah = you fast the day before; he eats with you after Maghrib, \"Allāhu akbar\".<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>38<\/td><td><b>15–21 May · ʿĪd al-Aḍḥā Sun 16 May<\/b><\/td><td>Sūrah al-Kawthar<\/td><td>namāz<\/td><td>ʿĪd prayer in the musallā — bring him, expect noise, the Prophet ﷺ brought children. Children watch the sacrifice from a distance, <b>no video of it<\/b>; meat ⅓ to the poor. <b>New toy: play kitchen + toy knife + soft fruit<\/b> so he \"helps\" at the chopping table, safely.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>39<\/td><td>22–28 May<\/td><td>review: al-Fātiḥah → al-Kawthar<\/td><td>takbīr<\/td><td>Ayyām at-Tashrīq: \"Allāhu akbar\" ringing through the house — dhikr as the background sound others fill with music.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 10 — Muharram 1449 · <b>1 Muharram ≈ Sun 6 Jun · ʿĀshūrāʾ ≈ Tue 15 Jun 2027<\/b> · <b>17 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: the Kalimah and the first \"fast\"<\/b> · <b>Ism: al-Awwal الأول<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>40<\/td><td>31 May–6 Jun<\/td><td>Sūrah Ibrāhīm 40<\/td><td>Kalimah / क़ल्मा<\/td><td><b>\"Lā ilāha illallāh\" 10× a day<\/b> in the house. Print it in Arabic + Urdu + English on the wall — a calligraphy card, no pictures.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>41<\/td><td><b>7–13 Jun · 1 Muharram Sun 6 Jun<\/b><\/td><td>Sūrah al-Fātiḥah<\/td><td>sāl (Hijri year)<\/td><td>New year: 2 rakʿah shukr, one ṣadaqah, write the duʿāʾ for his year in the diary. No resolutions party — this is the year that begins with Allāh.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>42<\/td><td><b>10 Muharram Tue 15 Jun<\/b><\/td><td>Sūrah ash-Sharḥ<\/td><td>rozā<\/td><td><b>First game-fast<\/b> on the 9th or 11th: he eats, then you say \"abhi nahi, Allāhu akbar\" and he waits till Ẓuhr. Not farḍ — identity. Plus one extra date for you both. For Karbalā: \"Sayyidunā Ḥusayn raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu, Allāh ke pyāre — unse mohabbat karo.\" No self-harm, no 3-day mourning atmosphere around a child; balance is sunnah.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>43<\/td><td>21–27 Jun<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Ḥujurāt 13<\/td><td>ḍuff / ढोलक<\/td><td><b>Rhythm day:<\/b> ḥamdh and ṣalāwāt with clapping + ḍuff, 5 min, twice a week. The daff was allowed for ʿīd and weddings — that is the frame; keep the home full of dhikr, not of sound.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 11 — Ṣafar 1449 · Jul 2027 · <b>18 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: tawakkul — Allāh is enough, no amulets<\/b> · <b>Ism: al-Ḥasīb الحسيب<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>44<\/td><td>28 Jun–4 Jul<\/td><td>Sūrah at-Tawbah 129<\/td><td>ḥifẓ / हफ़ज़<\/td><td>If someone offers a <i>taʿwīdh<\/i>, nazar bracelet, or evil-eye charm for the baby: decline politely. <i>\"Ḥasbunallāhu wa niʿma al-wakīl\"<\/i> and the Muʿawwidhatān are our protection. One calm sentence to the relatives, no argument.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>45<\/td><td>5–11 Jul<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Qalam 1–4<\/td><td>qalam / कलम · pen<\/td><td><b>New toy: 4-shape peg puzzle + a 12-book mini library.<\/b> 10 min of reading 2×/day: you point, he names.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>46<\/td><td>12–18 Jul<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Mulk 1–8<\/td><td>rāt / रात · night<\/td><td>al-Mulk audible as he sleeps. No fire-threat stories; at 18 months the seed you plant is <i>ar-Raḥmān<\/i>, not fear.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>47<\/td><td>19–25 Jul<\/td><td>review of 12 sūrahs<\/td><td>18-mo check<\/td><td><b>Should be:<\/b> 2-word phrases (\"pānī do\"), ~20 words, follows one-step orders, runs without falling, kicks a ball. <b>No words at all + no pointing = see the pediatrician this month<\/b>, don't \"wait and see\". Speech delay is treated easily at 18–24 mo.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Month 12 — Rabīʿ al-Awwal 1449 · Aug 2027 · <b>19 months<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><b>Theme: maḥabbat an-Nabī ﷺ — love, not ritual<\/b> · <b>Ism: ash-Shahīd الشهيد<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Wk<\/th><th>Dates<\/th><th>Āyah<\/th><th>Words<\/th><th>Do this<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>48<\/td><td>26 Jul–1 Aug<\/td><td>Sūrah Āl ʿImrān 31<\/td><td>muḥabbat / मोहब्बत<\/td><td>1 minute of his ﷺ life every night: he smiled at children, carried his grandsons on his back, was kind to servants, forgave Makkah. <i>This<\/i> is the Mawlid of a toddler.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>49<\/td><td>2–8 Aug<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Qāriʿah<\/td><td>sunnat<\/td><td>3 sunan in his body: siwāk/toothbrush in the right hand, right side for sleep, Bismillāh before food.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>50<\/td><td><b>9–15 Aug · Mawlid Sun 15 Aug 2027<\/b><\/td><td>Sūrah al-Fīl 1–5<\/td><td>ṣalāwat<\/td><td>Say <i>\"ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam\"<\/i> whenever his ﷺ name is mentioned — make it a reflex he hears all his life. Sweets to the neighbours in his name; 5 min ḥamd with ḍuff. No lights, no procession, no bidʿah you cannot explain to a 19-month-old.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>51<\/td><td>16–22 Aug<\/td><td>Sūrah al-Balad<\/td><td>ḥamd<\/td><td>Review: does he say Bismillāh / āmīn / Allāh? If yes — the year succeeded. If not, don't add toys: add <i>repetition<\/i> (say it 30× a day for a week, that's all).<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>52<\/td><td>23–29 Aug<\/td><td>plan for year 2<\/td><td>19-mo check<\/td><td><b>Buy for the 2nd year:<\/b> pull-wagon, 50 wooden blocks, DIY play-dough, doll + cup, mini broom, <b>his own prayer mat<\/b>, shaker/drum, sand set, toy knife + soft fruit. Then open <code>TOY-AND-STUDY-PLAN.md<\/code> §2 (1–2 y) and §3 (2–3 y).<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">C. Year-1 word bank — 24 words, three languages each<\/h2>\n<p><code>Allāh · Ummī · Abū · Bismillāh · Alḥamdulillāh · Allāhu akbar · SubḥānAllāh · āmīn · duʿā · namāz/salah · sajdah · adhān · ʿīd · Ramaḍān · rozā · ifṭār · ṣadaqah · Kaʿbah · pānī/water · dāhāṇā/right · sonā/sleep · khānā/food · jānvar/animal · kitāb/book · phool/flower<\/code> Say them <b>while doing the thing<\/b>, never as a test. 5 repetitions a day, 1 week per word, is enough at this age. <i>(Hindi/Urdu mix note: keep the dīn vocabulary in Arabic/Urdu — Allāh, namāz, roza, duʿā, āmīn. That is how the subcontinent kept ʿaqīdah clear for centuries, and it's easier for a child than two competing religious vocabularies.)<\/i><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">D. Duʿāʾ set for the 52 weeks<\/h2>\n<p>1. Before food: <i>Bismillāh<\/i> · if forgotten: <i>Bismillāhi fī kulli waḥtin wa ʿalā ḥālin<\/i> 2. After food: <i>Alḥamdulillāhi lladhī aṭʿamanā wa saqānā wa jaʿalanā muslimīn<\/i> 3. Sleep: <i>Bismik Allāhumma amūtu wa aḥyā<\/i> + 3 Qul + Āyat al-Kursī, blow into your hands, wipe over his body (the sunnah for small children) 4. <b>The Prophet's ﷺ duʿāʾ for al-Ḥasan &amp; al-Ḥusayn — on his head, every morning and every evening, all 52 weeks:<\/b> <i>Uʿīdhukā kalimāti Llāhi t-tāmmati min kulli shayṭānin wa hāmmatin, wa min kulli ʿaynin lāmmah.<\/i> 5. Morning: <i>Aṣbaḥnā wa aṣbaḥa l-mulku lillāh<\/i> · Evening: <i>Amsaynā wa amsā l-mulku lillāh<\/i> 6. Your own, in Urdu/Hindi — say it aloud near him often: <i>\"Allāh, Ḥanzalā ko ḥifẓ me rakh. Usko dīn aur duniyā me samajh de. Har buraī se bachā. Āmīn.\"<\/i><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">E. Sunday-night review — 2 minutes, one line in the diary<\/h2>\n<pre>Week __ | Āyah: ______ | Words he said: ______ | What was too much: ______ | Duʿāʾ for him by name: ☐ every day<\/pre>\n<p>If a week fails: <b>halve it<\/b>, don't abandon it. When you are exhausted, do the one thing left standing — duʿāʾ for him before Fajr. It is the heaviest item in this plan and the cheapest.<\/p>\n<hr>\n<p><i>May Allāh make Ḥanzalā the coolness of your eyes, shield him from every harm and every evil eye, put barakah in his years, and let him be among those who carry Your Book — and may you both be reunited with him in the highest Jannah. Āmīn. Wa ṣallā Llāhu ʿalā sayyidinā Muḥammadin wa ʿalā ālihi wa ṣaḥbihi wa sallam.<\/i><\/p>", "plan": "<h1 class=\"h1\">Hanzala — Toy &amp; Study Plan (with a Muslim angle)<\/h1>\n<p><b>Child's date of birth:<\/b> 11 January 2026 <b>Made:<\/b> 5 September 2026 — child is <b>7 months old<\/b> <b>How to use:<\/b> Work on the <i>current<\/i> age section only. Read the next section 1 month early so you are ready. Revisit every birthday. Everything here is <b>optional<\/b> — the sunnah is play and duʿāʾ, not buying things.<\/p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>Weekly schedule:<\/b> <code>WEEKLY-PLAN-YEAR1.md<\/code> — 52 weeks, Sep 2026 → Aug 2027 (āyah of the week, words, toys, Islamic dates)<\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">0. The 6 rules that matter more than any toy<\/h2>\n<p>1. <b>Your voice beats any product.<\/b> Reciting Qurʾān aloud in the house, dhikr while cooking, duʿāʾ before sleep — this is the #1 \"Islamic toy\" and it costs nothing. 2. <b>Halāl &amp; ṭayyib materials.<\/b> Choose wood, cotton, silicone, bamboo. Avoid strong chemical smell, soft PVC, and cheap batteries. Better for ʿaqīdah of the body (amānah) and for the dūnyā. 3. <b>Safety first — this is also dīn.<\/b> Harm (ḍarar) is forbidden. Under 3 years: no button batteries, no high-powered magnets, nothing that fits inside a toilet-paper roll (it fits in a throat). 4. <b>Fewer toys, more attention.<\/b> 5–8 toys out, rest hidden, rotate weekly. Clutter shortens attention span; a \"toy rotation\" feels like ʿīd every week. 5. <b>No screens before 18–24 months.<\/b> After that: max 15–20 min/day, only with you sitting beside him, never at suḥūr/iftār-style \"eating time\" and never 1 hour before sleep. 6. <b>Play is sunnah.<\/b> The Prophet ﷺ played with children, raced, carried his grandchildren on his back. Do not feel guilty about playing — it is ṣadaqah to your child.<\/p>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">1. Ages 0–12 months <i>(now → 11 Jan 2027)<\/i><\/h2>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">What his brain needs<\/h3>\n<p>Grasp → roll → sit → crawl → pull up. Learning = mouth + hands + ears.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Buy list (only these)<\/h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>#<\/th><th>Toy<\/th><th>Why<\/th><th>Age<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Black/white/red high-contrast cards or book<\/td><td>Newborn vision is built for contrast; calms and focuses<\/td><td>0–4 m<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>Soft fabric mirror (unbreakable)<\/td><td>First \"face\" game, self-recognition<\/td><td>2 m+<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>Crinkle cloth books (2–4)<\/td><td>Chewing + turning pages = hand-eye<\/td><td>3 m+<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>Wooden/ silicone rattles (2–3)<\/td><td>Cause &amp; effect, grip strength<\/td><td>3–6 m<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td>Teething: silicone ring, chilled (not frozen) cloth<\/td><td>Saves you both at 5–8 m<\/td><td>4 m+<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>Play mat + soft gym, or just a clean blanket on the floor<\/td><td>Tummy time is the single best \"exercise\"<\/td><td>0–12 m<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td>Soft ball (crinkle, 15 cm)<\/td><td>Rolling game = turn-taking, the first social skill<\/td><td>6 m+<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>8<\/td><td>Stacking cups (3–4, big) or wooden rings<\/td><td>Cup in cup = the first \"problem solved\"<\/td><td>8 m+<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>9<\/td><td>Simple busy board with 1 latch + 1 velcro<\/td><td>Finger dexterity, curiosity without danger<\/td><td>9–12 m<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>10<\/td><td>Bath toys: 3–4 cups, no holes (mould-free)<\/td><td>Water = sunnah of ṭahārah, clean fun<\/td><td>6 m+<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Skip / waste of money<\/h3>\n<p>Activity centres that lock him in, walker (banned by pediatricians, harms ṣibāh/legs), plush toys bigger than his head (sleep risk), anything with lights + sounds that he watches <i>instead of<\/i> doing the work, \"educational\" flash-card apps for babies.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Muslim-angle activities (10 min each, 3–4× a day)<\/h3>\n<ul><li><b>Talqīn of the sounds:<\/b> Recite <b>Aʿdān al-Ṣalāh / Sūrah al-Aʿlā / Yāsīn<\/b> softly near his ear after each ṣalāh. Babies learn the <i>music<\/i> of Arabic before the meaning — this is why ḥuffāẓ started as infants.<\/li><li><b>Kalimah loop:<\/b> Say <b>\"Lā ilāha illallāh, Muḥammadur Rasūlullāh\"<\/b> slowly 10× while rocking him. Repetition is the baby's whole curriculum.<\/li><li><b>Āyah of the week:<\/b> one short sūrah (al-Fātiḥah, al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq, an-Nās). You repeat it all day for every situation — while changing him, feeding, walking him to sleep.<\/li><li><b>Duʿāʾ of protection<\/b> on him each morning/evening: <i>Aʿūdhu bi-kalimāti Llāhi t-tāmmāti min kulli shayṭānin wa hāmmatin wa min kulli ʿaynin lāmmah.<\/i> (Abū Dāwūd) — wipe his head, duʿāʾ for ḥifẓ.<\/li><li><b>Naming duʿāʾ:<\/b> every time you call \"Yā Ḥanzalā!\" you are making duʿāʾ for him — call his name warmly, often, from across the room.<\/li><li><b>Ṣadaqah habit:<\/b> give him one biscuit/fruit piece and say \"Bismillāh\" — he can't do it yet, but the word becomes linked to food forever.<\/li><li><b>Sensational ḥalāl play:<\/b> roll the crinkle ball and say \"Allāhu akbar!\" when he catches it — praise with dhikr, not just \"good boy.\"<\/li><\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Daily rhythm template (7 months)<\/h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Time<\/th><th>What<\/th><th>Muslim angle<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Wake<\/td><td>Change, feed, open curtains<\/td><td>\"Alḥamdulillāhi lladhī aḥyānā baʿda mā amātanā\"<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>After Fajr<\/td><td>Floor play / tummy time + āyah of the week<\/td><td>Quiet brain hour — best for listening<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Mid-morning<\/td><td>Outside walk, touch leaves, water, soil<\/td><td>\"Tafakkur\" — point and say \"SubḥānAllāh\"<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Post-Ẓuhr<\/td><td>Nap + crinkle book<\/td><td>Play Sūrah softly, don't force sleep association<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Afternoon<\/td><td>Stacking cups / busy board / crawling obstacle<\/td><td>Say \"Bismillāh\" before play, \"Alḥamdulillāh\" after<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Maghrib<\/td><td>Family time, no screens<\/td><td>He sits in the majlis for 5 min — belonging<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>ʿIshāʾ<\/td><td>Bath → 3 min massage → bed<\/td><td>Duʿāʾ sleep + right side + 3 Qulūth<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">2. Ages 12–24 months <i>(11 Jan 2027 → 11 Jan 2028)<\/i><\/h2>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Buy list<\/h3>\n<ul><li><b>Wooden blocks, 40–60 pieces<\/b> (the single highest-value toy of childhood)<\/li><li><b>Push-pull wagon / trolley<\/b> (not a walker — he is already walking)<\/li><li><b>Large soft building blocks / card-box bricks<\/b> — build &amp; destroy, he'll love it<\/li><li><b>Shape sorter<\/b> (circle, square, triangle only at first)<\/li><li><b>Stacking ring, 6 discs<\/b> + <b>nesting boxes<\/b><\/li><li><b>Play-dough (flour + salt + oil + water recipe — you make it, so it's ḥalāl and safe if eaten)<\/b><\/li><li><b>Toy knife + soft fruits/veg for cutting<\/b> (Velcro fruit)<\/li><li><b>Mini broom, small towel, jug<\/b> — <i>chores as toys<\/i>, deeply Islamic<\/li><li><b>Musical: wooden shaker, small drum, bells<\/b> (rhythmic, keep it acoustic)<\/li><li><b>Books — 10 favourites, hardboard:<\/b> animals, vehicles, body parts, bedtime, Muslims-pray style board books<\/li><li><b>Chunky crayons (triangular) + paper taped to the wall<\/b><\/li><li><b>Sand/water play: 2 buckets + 1 jug + spoons<\/b> (outdoor, best 20-min time-killer)<\/li><li><b>Doll + small blanket + cup<\/b> (for mercy-training — see below)<\/li><li><b>Puzzle: 3–6 piece knob puzzles, wooden<\/b><\/li><li><b>Ride-on (small, feet on floor) + helmet from 18 m<\/b><\/li><li><b>First prayer-rug the right size<\/b> (his own, ~90 cm)<\/li><\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Skip<\/h3>\n<p>Electronic \"teaches ABC 123\" tablets, licensed-character toys at this age, anything with small removable parts, trampolines, toy weapons with sharp edges.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Muslim-angle activities<\/h3>\n<ul><li>**Pray <i>at<\/i> him, not <i>at<\/i> the TV:** lay his rug, stand him beside you, put his little forehead down when you say sujud. Copying prayer is the learning method of this age — do not correct, do not interrupt.<\/li><li><b>Adhkār as games:<\/b><\/li><li>Bismillāh → before food, before play, before getting in the car<\/li><li>Alḥamdulillāh → after eating, after sneezing, after a finished tower<\/li><li>Allāhu akbar → when he sees something big (dog, plane, mountain, your prayer)<\/li><li>SubḥānAllāh → the sky, the moon, the baby cousin, rain<\/li><li>Āmīn → after any duʿāʾ you make out loud for him<\/li><li><b>Aḍḥáḥá (mercy) training:<\/b> he must be gentle with the doll, the cat, the ants. Hadith: <i>\"The one who is not merciful to our young is not of us.\"<\/i> When he hits the doll, don't shout — take his hand and stroke the doll: \"Be soft, inshāʾAllāh.\"<\/li><li><b>Sharākah (sharing) games:<\/b> 2 biscuits, \"one for you, one for Ummī\"; the toy must be given back. Practise now, no lecture later.<\/li><li><b>Tahārah play:<\/b> let him pour water over your hands, wash his own feet before bed. \"Cleanliness is half of faith\" becomes muscle memory.<\/li><li><b>Ṣadaqah box at home:<\/b> a small tin; each week he puts in one coin (or one fruit for the neighbour). Say duʿāʾ when he gives.<\/li><li><b>Names of Allāh, 1 per month:<\/b> ar-Raḥmān, al-Wāḥid, as-Samīʿ, al-Bāṣir, al-Khāliq… Say it 10× while pointing at what it means (\"Allāh is al-Bāṣir — He sees your little car under the chair!\").<\/li><li><b>First \"study\":<\/b> 5 min, 2×/day. Only this: 4 letters (ا ب ت ث or his own name letters), 1 sūrah, 1 animal sound, 1 colour. Sit with him, do not test him.<\/li><\/ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">3. Ages 2–3 years <i>(11 Jan 2028 → 11 Jan 2029)<\/i><\/h2>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Buy list<\/h3>\n<ul><li><b>Duplo-style big bricks<\/b> + <b>wooden train set + track<\/b> (the two toys with the longest play-life)<\/li><li><b>Puzzles 10–20 pieces<\/b>, <b>magnetic wooden puzzle letters<\/b><\/li><li><b>Dress-up:<\/b> thobe/kurta + shawl, firefighter, doctor, animal masks (identity play, empathy)<\/li><li><b>Play kitchen + dishes + real small jug<\/b> (he serves you; adab of serving)<\/li><li><b>Balance bike<\/b> (better than a tricycle; helmet always) + <b>sandbox set<\/b><\/li><li><b>Art station:<\/b> washable poster paint, chunky brushes, 3 sizes of paper, glue stick, safety scissors<\/li><li><b>Play-dough tools + rolling pin + real cookie cutters<\/b><\/li><li><b>Marble run / wooden ramp cars<\/b> (early physics, no battery)<\/li><li><b>Board games of the simple kind:<\/b> first cooperative games, dominoes, memory card pairs (animals)<\/li><li><b>A \"little library\" of 25 books:<\/b> prophets' stories for small ones, ḥadīth-of-the-week style, emotions books, nature books, Arabic alphabet books<\/li><li><b>Qurbāni play set (pretend animals + no knife)<\/b> — for ʿĪd understanding<\/li><li><b>Hajj sandbox play:<\/b> sand, small stones, boxes = kaʿbah, ʿarafah tent (build it together on Dhū al-Ḥijjah 9)<\/li><li><b>First \"own\" things<\/b>: own miswāk/toothbrush, own small towel, own prayer rug, own bag<\/li><\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Muslim-angle activities<\/h3>\n<ul><li><b>Ṣalāh with ṭumaʾnīnah:<\/b> start teaching the <i>positions<\/i>, one per week. Use a chart with pictures on the wall. Never force more than 2 rakʿahs with you; \"who finishes with Ummī gets a hug + date.\"<\/li><li><b>Sūrah progress:<\/b> al-Mulk + as-Sajdah at night (sunnah before sleep) + Juz ʿAmma short sūrahs. Target: <b>15 short sūrahs by age 3<\/b> (al-Fātiḥah → aḍ-Ḍuḥā).<\/li><li><b>Ruwā of the prophets (child-safe):<\/b> 3 min each night — Ādam, Nūḥ (the ship!), Ibrāhīm (the fire that became a garden), Yūsuf, Mūsā (the sea), Yūnus (the whale), ʿĪsā, Muḥammad ﷺ (his birth, his kindness to children). Retell orally, do not skip; do not draw the prophets.<\/li><li><b>First fast, symbolically:<\/b> half day on ʿĀshūrāʾ and the white days, plus Ramadān \"until Ẓuhr.\" Give a plate for suḥūr — the memory matters more than the hunger.<\/li><li><b>Two ʿīds as projects:<\/b> 3 days before, make a card, choose the clothes, give ṣadaqah, visit the neighbour. Write a \"ʿīd checklist\" with his photo.<\/li><li><b>Adab curriculum (behaviour, not knowledge):<\/b> sneezing duʿāʾ, knocking 3× and saying salām before entering, not eating left-handed, saying \"Ummī/Abū\" kindly, no shouting in the house, greeting the neighbours, kissing grandparents' hands.<\/li><li><b>Qiyām of the heart:<\/b> wake him 5 min before Fajr once a week, make duʿāʾ with his hands up, one date, then back to bed. \"Yā Allāh, help Ḥanzalā.\"<\/li><li><b>Nature as a madrasah:<\/b> monthly trip — sea/river, farm, mountain, market. Rule: he must bring back 1 leaf/1 stone and you ask \"who made this?\" (al-Khāliq).<\/li><li><b>Animal mercy day:<\/b> feed birds, put out water for insects; the woman in the ḥadīth who was punished for a cat, and the man forgiven for giving a thirsty dog water — tell both stories at 2.5+.<\/li><li><b>Study plan, 10–15 min × 2/day:<\/b> hijāʾ letters (all 28 by 3.5), write in sand/flour/tray (no pencils yet), count to 20 with beads, sort by colour/shape, name body parts in Arabic, one new English word per day with you speaking it (not an app).<\/li><\/ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">4. Ages 3–5 years <i>(11 Jan 2029 → 11 Jan 2031)<\/i> — the golden years of memory<\/h2>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Buy list<\/h3>\n<ul><li><b>Qurʾān: one mushaf for the house + one kid-friendly Qāʿidah<\/b> (Nūrānī Qāʿidah / al-Baghī / Madinī Primer / Qāʿidah al-Fātiḥah — pick ONE and stick with it)<\/li><li><b>Arabic letter magnets + sand tray for handwriting<\/b><\/li><li><b>Blocks: wooden unit blocks, Lego/Duplo, magnets (as a set, not hundreds of pieces)<\/b><\/li><li><b>Real tools play: small hammer + wooden planks + safety goggles, screwdriver set<\/b> (Amānah on hands; also builds focus)<\/li><li><b>Jigsaw 40–80 pieces<\/b>, <b>Sudoku for kids<\/b>, <b>pattern blocks<\/b><\/li><li><b>Sewing/cards: laminated āyah-matching cards, \"build a word\" cards<\/b><\/li><li>**Musical: oud/qanun <i>or<\/i> a real beginner percussion (duff/ṭar only, keep it simple)**, plus a recorder if you want an instrument<\/li><li><b>Bicycle with pedals at 4<\/b>, swimming lessons at 4 (sunnah skill: swimming, archery-style target games, running races)<\/li><li><b>Board games:<\/b> snakes &amp; ladders, ludo, Checkers/English draughts (kids version), Story Cubes, Blokus junior<\/li><li><b>Science-lite toys:<\/b> kids microscope, magnets, bug box, water filter/sprouting kit, dominoes<\/li><li><b>World play:<\/b> prayer beads (his own misbaḥah, 33), hijab/prayer set for family, small kaʿbah model, Makkah/Madinah picture book<\/li><li><b>A \"work desk\" of his own<\/b>, 30 min of sitting, 1 chair, 1 lamp — the desk is the respect for learning<\/li><\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Muslim-angle activities<\/h3>\n<ul><li><b>The 5-per-day structure, not the count:<\/b> he prays <i>with<\/i> the family, and you ask afterwards \"what did you say to Allāh?\" Not a quiz — a chat.<\/li><li><b>Qurʾān ḥalqah at home:<\/b> after Fajr or Maghrib, 20 min, sit with the mushaf, listen first, then repeat. Do not rush reading — correct pronunciation <i>now<\/i> is a gift for life.<\/li><li><b>Ḥifẓ target (realistic, no pressure):<\/b> Juz ʿAmma by 5, Sūrah al-Mulk by 5.5. 5 new āyāt a day, revise 3 days. If he resists for 2 weeks, stop and restart — never make Qurʾān a punishment; that is how children grow up hating it.<\/li><li><b>40 ḥadīths of the small:<\/b> An-Nawawī's 42→ choose 10 for the year: actions by intentions, cleanliness is half of faith, be not angry, smile is ṣadaqah, feed the hungry, seek knowledge, honour your mother, no harm, good character, duʿāʾ.<\/li><li><b>Aḥl al-Bayt &amp; ṣaḥābah as friends:<\/b> tell stories of Fāṭimah az-Zahrāʾ, al-Ḥasan &amp; al-Ḥusayn, Bilāl, Khadījah, ʿUmar's justice, Ṣalāḥ ad-Dīn's kindness — one each Friday after ʿIshāʾ, 5 min.<\/li><li><b>Friday ritual (Jumuʿah):<\/b> bath + thobe + smell good + go to the musalla (even if he plays outside the row) + one sūrah al-Kahf ayah read by Abū + give coins in the box + lunch is special. This single routine creates the identity of a Muslim man/boy more than any lesson.<\/li><li><b>Ramadān plan for 4–5:<\/b> suḥūr with the family, one ṣawm a week, help lay the table for iftār, count the misbaḥah after tarāwīḥ, \"Quran khatm chart\" with stars, last 10 nights — wake for Qadr once, and let him \"watch\" the duʿāʾ.<\/li><li><b>Charity with his own hands:<\/b> choose 1 of his toys/clothes and give them; take him to distribute a meal once per Ramadān. Teach \"the hand that gives.\"<\/li><li><b>Guardianship of speech (ḥifẓ al-lisān):<\/b> no swearing at home, no \"I hate\", no lying even about a broken cup — praise truth-telling <i>after<\/i> a mistake: \"You told me the truth — that is the best thing, now we clean it together.\"<\/li><li><b>Screen rule, hard line:<\/b> only after Qurʾān and homework; max 30 min/day; 1 shared show per week with the family (e.g. a Prophets-style animated series) and you discuss it; no device in the bedroom, no device at meals, no device before Fajr. Use a filter/router schedule — parents control the wifi.<\/li><li><b>Study blocks (30–40 min, split):<\/b> Arabic letters + Qurʾān 15, numbers 20/100/counting objects 10, English phonics (read to him nightly) 10, one worksheet 5. Everything with a <i>physical<\/i> object in the hand.<\/li><\/ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">5. Ages 6–10 (school years) — quick forward map<\/h2>\n<ul><li><b>Skills to buy, not toys:<\/b> swimming (must), archery/target &amp; fencing-style games, cycling, horse/pool/skate, one team sport, first <i>real<\/i> responsibility: his own lunch box, his own bag, wake himself for Fajr.<\/li><li><b>Islamic syllabus by age 10:<\/b> ʿaqīdah of the 6 imān (in his own words), fiqh of ṭahārah &amp; ṣalāh &amp; fasting &amp; ḥajj (do ʿumrah with him — the best \"field trip\" in Islam), sīrah of the Prophet ﷺ cover to cover in child books, 20 chosen duʿāʾ of morning/evening, sūrah al-Baqarah recitation progress, Arabic grammar starting with al-Ājurrūmiyyah-lite, one <i>seerah biography<\/i> read per month.<\/li><li><b>One weekly \"dars\" with Abū:<\/b> Thursday after Maghrib, 45 min, tea + biscuits, 1 ḥadīth + 1 real-life challenge for the week (\"this week, no anger\").<\/li><li><b>Money &amp; ḥalāl:<\/b> give a small weekly allowance, 3 jars: spend / ṣadaqah / save. No interest talk needed yet, but \"we don't buy games with the ṣadaqah jar.\"<\/li><li><b>Friendship filter:<\/b> know the names of 5 friends and their parents; host them at home (you can see what they watch). \"A man is on the dīn of his friend.\"<\/li><li>**Teach him to <i>make<\/i> things:** sewing a button, tying a knot, fixing a bike, cooking 3 dishes by 10, using a knife, cleaning after himself. Competence is ʿizzah.<\/li><\/ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">6. What to AVOID — dīn and safety reasons<\/h2>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Avoid<\/th><th>Why<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Toys with shirk symbols (crosses as decoration, statues to venerate, magic/wizard \"power\" games, tarot-style cards, evil-eye amulets as toy accessories)<\/td><td>Protection of tawḥīd — the mind at 3–7 accepts pictures as truth<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>\"God is a baby\", \"Jesus plays football\" style books, and any story that says Allāh has a son<\/td><td>Fix ʿaqīdah before story-time<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Music-heavy electronic toys that replace talking; loud sound toys (&gt;85 dB harms infant hearing)<\/td><td>Hearing is amānah; speech delay is real<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Toy guns/realistic weapons, cartoon characters known for vulgarity<\/td><td>Keep it clean<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Music/singing — the scholarly position differs, so the safe path: <b>duʿāʾ, nasheeds without instruments, ṭar/duff at ʿīd and weddings, Qurʾān, poems of ḥikmah.<\/b> Be moderate, don't make the home silent like a graveyard, and don't fill it with loud clubs<\/td><td>Ijtihād area — follow your madhhab/scholar and be balanced<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Anime/cartoons with sexualised characters, or the \"free apps\" full of ads<\/td><td>Lower the gaze, protect the mind; parents filter<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Music/beats while sleeping, videos as a babysitter<\/td><td>Sleep &amp; attention are sunnah rights<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Gold/silk for him as a boy later (and anything imitating the opposite sex in play)<\/td><td>Fiqh of clothing, teach naturally at 5–6<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Dogs as indoor pets, pig-themed toys<\/td><td>Najāsah/ḥukm — explain simply, no shaming<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Halloween, birthday \"cake worship\", Christmas toys, Valentine's stuff, magic trick \"spells\"<\/td><td>Muslim identity — teach him he has two ʿīds of his own<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Small batteries, magnets, marbles under age 3; button batteries = emergency<\/td><td>Ḍarar is forbidden; keep them out of the house<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unrestricted YouTube<\/td><td>Nothing helps a 4-year-old more than the removal of autoplay<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">7. The \"buy once\" master list (print this)<\/h2>\n<p><b>0–12 m:<\/b> contrast cards · fabric mirror · 3 crinkle books · 2 rattles · teether · play mat · crinkle ball · 4 stacking cups · 6 soft blocks · bath cups <b>1–2 y:<\/b> 50 wooden blocks · pull wagon · shape sorter · busy board · play-dough · cutting fruit · mini broom · drum/shaker · 10 board books · crayons · sand set · doll + cup · own prayer mat <b>2–3 y:<\/b> Duplo · train + track · 12-piece puzzles · dress-up · play kitchen · balance bike · poster paint + paper · play-dough tools · marble ramp · dominoes/memory cards · 25 books · kaʿbah &amp; ʿīd play bits <b>3–5 y:<\/b> mushaf + Qāʿidah · Arabic magnets + sand tray · Lego/magnets · real-tool kit · 60-piece jigsaws · misbaḥah · bike · beginner sport gear · board games · kids microscope · desk &amp; lamp · 40 books (sīrah/ḥadīth/emotions/science) <b>6–10 y:<\/b> team sport kit · swimming lessons · archery/skate/pool · first real books (sīrah, prophets, Islamic history, encyclopaedia) · 3 money jars · workshop/repair box · library card · one musical-free instrument or nasheed group<\/p>\n<p><b>Budget tip:<\/b> 70% of this is achievable with wooden second-hand toys, market stalls, DIY play-dough, and free nature play. Spend on the <b>blocks, the mushaf/Qāʿidah, the bike, the books, and the experiences<\/b> — not on lights, licences, and sounds.<\/p>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">8. Daily / weekly / yearly checklist<\/h2>\n<p><b>Every day (must-dos, all free):<\/b><\/p>\n<ul><li>☐ Bismillāh before food &amp; play · ☐ Alḥamdulillāh after · ☐ 10 min Qurʾān audible · ☐ 1 ṣalāh together · ☐ 30 min outdoor/ḥaraj-free movement · ☐ 15 min reading to him · ☐ evening adhkār · ☐ duʿāʾ for him with his name, hands on his head · ☐ no screens before sleep<\/li><\/ul>\n<p><b>Every week:<\/b> ☐ one new āyah/ḥadīth · ☐ ṣadaqah with his hand · ☐ Jumuʿah for the boy (from 5) · ☐ toy rotation · ☐ 1 family visit / relatives (ṣilat ar-raḥim)<\/p>\n<p><b>Every month:<\/b> ☐ measure &amp; log milestones (below) · ☐ 1 \"big experience\" (farm, sea, museum, masjid, market, park) · ☐ 1 new book series · ☐ check toy safety: broken parts, loose eyes, batteries<\/p>\n<p><b>Every year:<\/b> ☐ ʿāfiyah duʿāʾ on his birthday (the <i>shukr<\/i> of another year, not a party) — fasting or ṣadaqah, and a written duʿāʾ letter to him for the next year · ☐ ḥifẓ review with the teacher · ☐ doctor, eyes, teeth · ☐ re-write this plan for the new age<\/p>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">9. Milestone checklists — if 2+ items miss in one age, see your pediatrician<\/h2>\n<p><b>Development (WHO/AAP style):<\/b><\/p>\n<ul><li><b>6 m:<\/b> sits with support · laughs · reaches for toys · turns to his name · babbles \"ba da\"<\/li><li><b>12 m:<\/b> pulls to stand · 1–3 words · points with finger · waves bye · crawls/cruises · looks where you point<\/li><li><b>18 m:<\/b> walks well · ~10–20 words · 2-block tower · pretends with a doll · follows 1-step instruction<\/li><li><b>24 m:<\/b> 2-word phrases · ~50+ words · runs, kicks · parallel play · removes socks/shoes<\/li><li><b>36 m:<\/b> 3–4-word sentences · jumps with both feet · turns pages · asks \"what's that?\" · copies a circle<\/li><li><b>48 m:<\/b> tells a short story · hops on one foot · copies a cross/square · counts 4 objects · washes hands<\/li><li><b>60 m:<\/b> knows some letters · ties knots with string · counts 10 · takes turns in a game · recites short sūrahs<\/li><\/ul>\n<p><b>Muslim milestones (a nice, gentle chart):<\/b><\/p>\n<ul><li><b>1 y:<\/b> responds to \"Assalāmu ʿalaykum\" greeting · calms when the āyah voice is heard<\/li><li><b>2 y:<\/b> says \"Allāh\" / \"duʿāʾ\" · makes a shape of sujud · says Bismillāh when reminded<\/li><li><b>3 y:<\/b> finishes \"Alḥamdulillāhi…\" after a sneeze · points at the sky and says \"Allāh\" · loves the adhān<\/li><li><b>4 y:<\/b> recites al-Fātiḥah with you · knows Makkah is the kaʿbah · asks \"why do we fast?\"<\/li><li><b>5 y:<\/b> stands in ṣalāh for the full positions · memorises 5+ short sūrahs · knows the 5 daily ṣalāh names · reads hijāʾ letters<\/li><li><b>6 y:<\/b> recites al-Fātiḥah correctly, knows the meaning of Kalimat at-Tawḥīd<\/li><li><b>7 y:<\/b> asked to pray (the age of the command in the sunnah) · begins regular Qurʾān lessons<\/li><li><b>9–10 y:<\/b> prays 5 on his own without being told · can name 6 imān · fasts Ramadān fully when able<\/li><\/ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">10. The duʿāʾ to keep for him (write these on the fridge)<\/h2>\n<p>1. <i>Rabbi-jʿalnī muqīma ṣ-ṣalāti wa min dhurriyyatī, Rabbanā wa taqabbal duʿāʾ.<\/i> (Ibrāhīm 14:40) 2. <i>Rabbanā hab lanā min azwājinā wa dhurriyyātinā qurrata aʿyunin wajʿalnā lil-muttaqīna imāmā.<\/i> (al-Furqān 25:74) 3. <i>Allāhumma innī asʾaluka ʿilman nāfiʿan wa rizqan ṭayyiban wa ʿamalan mutaqabbalā.<\/i> 4. <i>Allāhumma ḥaffiẓ Ḥanzalā wa ijʿalhu qurrata ʿaynin lī, ḥāfidhan li-kitābika, ʿāmilan bi-sunnati nabiyyika.<\/i> (your own — make it in your language too; Allāh understands all) 5. <i>Allāhumma innī aʿūdhu bika an yatakhabbalani sh-shayṭānu ʿinda awājinī…<\/i> — protection duʿāʾ for children (recite over him, as the Prophet ﷺ did for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn)<\/p>\n<hr>\n<h3 class=\"h3\">Final word<\/h3>\n<p>The best toy is <b>Abū on the floor for 20 minutes<\/b> and <b>Ummī's voice reciting at night<\/b>. The best \"study list\" is <b>one sūrah, one ḥadīth, one kind act — every week, for ten years.<\/b> Buy less, be present more, make duʿāʾ constantly, and Allāh is the One who grants righteous offspring — <i>\"Lā ilāha illā Anta subḥānaka innī kuntu mina ẓ-ẓālimīn\"<\/i> — and He changes hearts. May Allāh make Ḥanzala the coolness of your eyes, protect him, and make him among the ahl al-Qurʾān. Āmīn.<\/p>", "fridge": "<h1 class=\"h1\">Fridge Sheet — Hanzala (born 11 Jan 2026)<\/h1>\n<p>Print on A4, tape it next to the kitchen. This is the whole plan in one page.<\/p>\n<p><b>Weekly schedule:<\/b> <code>WEEKLY-PLAN-YEAR1.md<\/code> — 52 weeks, Sep 2026 → Aug 2027 (āyah of the week, words, toys, Islamic dates)<\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">THIS YEAR'S ISLAMIC DATES (mark them)<\/h2>\n<p>Ramaḍān <b>8 Feb 27<\/b> · ʿĪd al-Fiṭr <b>9–10 Mar<\/b> · ʿArafah <b>15 May<\/b> · ʿĪd al-Aḍḥā <b>16 May<\/b> · 1 Muharram <b>6 Jun<\/b> · ʿĀshūrāʾ <b>15 Jun<\/b> · <b>Mawlid 15 Aug 27<\/b> · his 1st year: <b>11 Jan 27 = shukr day, not a cake-party<\/b><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">NOW (7 months → 1 year)<\/h2>\n<p><b>3 toys out at a time:<\/b> soft ball · stacking cups · crinkle book. Rotate weekly. <b>Every day:<\/b><\/p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> Qurʾān audible in the house (al-Mulk / Juz ʿAmma loop) — 10 min<\/li><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> \"Lā ilāha illallāh\" × 10 while rocking<\/li><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> Āyah of the week: ______________________<\/li><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> Say <b>Bismillāh<\/b> before food · <b>Alḥamdulillāh<\/b> after · <b>Allāhu akbar<\/b> at something big · <b>SubḥānAllāh<\/b> at sky/animals<\/li><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> Protection duʿāʾ morning + evening, hand on his head<\/li><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> Tummy time 15 min · floor play 45 min · outside walk 30 min<\/li><li><span class=\"tick\"><\/span> <b>No screens.<\/b> No walker. No small parts. No button batteries.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">THIS YEAR'S LEARNING LIST (0–12 m)<\/h2>\n<p>1. Al-Fātiḥah  2. Al-Ikhlāṣ  3. Al-Falaq  4. An-Nās  5. Al-Kawthar 6. \"Āmīn\"  7. \"Āmīn\" after duʿāʾ  8. Salam response  9. His own name  10. Waving bye-bye<\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">1–2 years, buy only these<\/h2>\n<p>50 wooden blocks · pull wagon · shape sorter · play-dough (DIY) · toy knife + soft fruit · <b>mini broom + small towel<\/b> · drum/shaker · 10 board books · crayons · sand bucket set · doll + cup · <b>his own small prayer rug<\/b><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">DAILY 10-MINUTE MUSLIM ROUTINES (any age)<\/h2>\n<ul><li><b>Sujud copy:<\/b> he lays his forehead down when you do<\/li><li><b>Gentleness:<\/b> stroke the doll/cat/ant — \"be soft\"<\/li><li><b>Sharing:<\/b> 2 biscuits — \"one for you, one for Ummī\"<\/li><li><b>Wudu help:<\/b> he pours water on your hands<\/li><li><b>Ṣadaqah tin:<\/b> 1 coin per week, his hand, then duʿāʾ<\/li><li><b>Name of Allāh of the month:<\/b> ______________________<\/li><li><b>Bedtime:<\/b> 3 Qul + duʿāʾ sleep + right side, wipe over him<\/li><\/ul>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">AGE 3: 15 short sūrahs · AGE 4: Qāʿidah letters · AGE 5: Juz ʿAmma + ṣalāh positions<\/h2>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">AGE 7: start the command of ṣalāh · Qurʾān lessons 4×/week<\/h2>\n<h2 class=\"h2\">THE 6 THINGS THAT ACTUALLY RAISE A MUSLIM CHILD<\/h2>\n<p>1. Parents praying visibly, every day, at home 2. Qurʾān heard, not just taught 3. Duʿāʾ for him by name, often, especially at tahajjud 4. Mercy in the house — no shouting, no hitting, no sarcasm 5. Two ʿīds, Jumuʿah, Ramadān, family visits = the year's rhythm 6. Guarded eyes and ears: parent-controlled wifi, no autoplay, no unsupervised YouTube<\/p>\n<blockquote>\"Rabbanā hab lanā min azwājinā wa dhurriyyātinā qurrata aʿyunin wajʿalnā lil-muttaqīna imāmā.\" (25:74)<\/blockquote>"};
